Guess History Landing Page Specification v2.0

Project: guess-history.com

Objective

Create a premium cinematic landing page that explains the game through interactive scrollytelling, builds trust in AI-generated historical reconstructions, and converts visitors into players in under 60 seconds.

The experience should feel like an interactive documentary rather than a traditional marketing page.

Primary Goals
Explain the game in less than one minute.
Create curiosity immediately.
Demonstrate gameplay visually.
Build trust in AI-generated imagery.
Convert visitors into players.

Success metric:

Visitor reaches first Play Free CTA before 60 seconds.

Target Audience
Curious people
Casual gamers
History enthusiasts
Quiz players
Educational users
Mobile-first users
Design Philosophy
Minimal Prose

Large editorial typography.

Very little text.

Every sentence must earn its place.

Maximum Drama

The images tell the story.

Scrolling reveals information progressively.

Never overwhelm users with paragraphs.

User-Controlled Motion

Animations are entirely scroll-driven.

No autoplay cinematic sequences.

